' Hayai escrow payment flow — open / settle / protest / refundInactive.
' Companion to proto/SPEC.md §3a (ticket lifecycle, settlement asset model,
' operator authentication, settlement windows) and §3b (slashing evidence).
' Contract methods sourced from proto/escrow/ZeroSignalEscrow.arc56.json.
'
' This diagram reflects the consensus-verified-operator + prepaid-MBR-pool
' design (SPEC.md "Operator authentication" + "Settlement asset model"):
'   * open()  is a 2-tx group [payer usdcPayment + operator-signed AppCall];
'             the operator's gtxn[1] carries fee = 2 * minTxnFee to fee-pool
'             the whole group. There is NO feePayment leg — the box MBR is
'             drawn from the payer's prepaid pool (open() does openTickets++).
'   * settle() is normally an atomic 2-tx group [op_first_half + payer_ack];
'             gtxn[0] (operator-signed) fee-pools the group, SIZED to the
'             disbursement inners that actually fire (escrow/fee.go):
'               fee = (2 outer + SettleInnerCount + gapOpUps) * minTxnFee
'             SettleInnerCount = 0..3 (0 for a free model, 1 for a 0-charge
'             refund, 3 for a paid ticket that also refunds). The grouped path
'             issues NO base op-up, so a steady-state paid settle = 5 and a
'             free-model settle = 2; gapOpUps (>0 only across revenue-ring day
'             gaps) reaches ~6 in the worst case.
'   * Standalone settle / settleLapsed: single app call, so it DOES add a base
'             op-up: fee = (1 outer + SettleInnerCount + 1 base op-up + gapOpUps)
'             * minTxnFee — 5 for a paid ticket, 2 for a free model.
'   * Payer ALGO net cost on the happy path is 0 microALGO. Operator
'     absorbs ~8,000 microALGO/request, recovered through USDC rates.
'     (The box-MBR ALGO is a one-time recoverable per-payer pool deposit
'      via depositMbr, not a per-turn cost.)

@startuml flow-escrow-payment
title Hayai escrow lifecycle — payment, settlement, protest, refund

autonumber "<b>[00]</b>"
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #444
    LifeLineBorderColor #888
    ParticipantBorderColor #444
    NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
    NoteBorderColor #C0A000
}

actor       "Payer\n(end-user wallet)"                        as Payer
participant "Proxy\n(client-side signer,\nhayai_dispatch.go)" as Proxy
participant "Escrow App\nZeroSignalEscrow.arc56.json\n(Ticket + Operator + Node boxes)"   as Escrow
participant "Serving Node\n(one node within an operator)\nreserve.go + tickets.go +\nreceipt.go + settlement worker" as Operator

note over Escrow
  TicketRecord fields (proto/escrow/ZeroSignalEscrow.arc56.json):
    payer, operatorId, nodeId, operatorOwner (operator-box payout),
    nodeSigning (the serving node's key, from the node box),
    maxPrice, openedAt, expiresAt, settlementGraceSeconds,
    status, pendingAmount, pendingBy, pendingDigest, commitK
  STATUS values: OPEN=1, FROZEN=4, PENDING_SETTLE=5
  (SETTLED=2 / REFUNDED=3 are never stored — those paths delete the box.)
  pendingBy: NONE=0, OPERATOR=1, PAYER=2
end note

== Admission (see flow-ticket-reserve) ==

Payer -> Proxy: /v1/chat/completions (plaintext)
Proxy -> Operator: POST /v1/zs/reserve\n{model, input_tokens, max_output_tokens, stream,\n proxy_recipient, payer_addr}
Operator --> Proxy: signed Ticket + wrapped_response_key\n+ presigned_open_txn (operator-signed gtxn[1],\n  fee=2*minTxnFee, ABI args carry payer_addr)

== 1. Payment — open escrow ticket (consensus-verified operator) ==

note over Proxy, Operator
  Co-composed open group (2 txns — NO feePayment leg):
    gtxn[0]  payer usdcPayment  ASA   amount = max_price       fee = 0
              receiver = escrow app addr,  asset = usdcAssetId
    gtxn[1]  node AppCall       open(operatorId, nodeId, maxPrice,
                                    expiresAt, payerAddr,
                                    settlementGraceSeconds, commitK)
              sender = the serving node's signing key (nodeSigning),
                       fee = 2 * minTxnFee
  The operator's gtxn[1] is delivered at reserve time as
  presigned_open_txn; the proxy signs gtxn[0] against the group hash
  already pinned into gtxn[1] (no re-signing of gtxn[1]). The box MBR
  is drawn from the payer's prepaid pool (depositMbr'd earlier) —
  open() does openTickets++ to claim one slot from the pool.
end note

Proxy -> Proxy: SubmitPresignedOpenGroup\n  decode presigned_open_txn -> SignedTxn for gtxn[1]\n  build gtxn[0] usdcPayment (sender=payer, fee=0) per the\n  shape pinned at reserve time\n  sign gtxn[0] with payer key\n  assemble [gtxn0, gtxn1] and broadcast atomically
Proxy -> Escrow: submit signed 2-tx group
Escrow -> Escrow: open()  (ZeroSignalEscrow.algo.ts::open)\n  resolve the serving node from the (operatorId, nodeId) node box\n  consensus check: Txn.sender == nodeRecord.signing (node's hot key)\n  (Algorand pool admission verifies the node's Ed25519 sig over the\n   canonical txn bytes — no in-contract ed25519verify_bare;\n   "consensus-verified operator")\n  require usdcPayment.assetAmount == max_price\n  require payer opted-in AND\n          (openTickets + 1) * mbrForTicket() <= algoBalance\n  openTickets++  (draw one box-MBR slot from the prepaid pool)\n  bind t.payer = payerAddr (from ABI arg, NOT Txn.Sender)\n  snapshot operatorId, nodeId, operatorOwner (operator-box payout),\n           nodeSigning (node-box key) onto the TicketRecord\n  create TicketRecord box keyed by ticket_id;  status = STATUS_OPEN
Escrow --> Proxy: per-tx txids (gtxn[0], gtxn[1]) + group id
Proxy -> Proxy: gtxn[1] app-call txid threaded into the\n  inner-request header's algorand_tx_id (inside the seal)\n  (group id retained on OpenHandle for audit only;\n   see flow-request-response)

== 2. Inference round-trip ==

note over Proxy, Operator #lightgray
  Sealed request / response choreography is covered by
  flow-request-response.puml. The operator emits:
    - signed UsageReceipt   (X-Zs-Receipt header /
                             event: zs-receipt SSE frame)
    - operator-signed atomic settle group, gtxn[0] only
                            (X-Zs-Settle-Group header /
                             event: zs-settle-group SSE frame)
  The proxy completes gtxn[1] of the settle group (payer ack)
  for atomic broadcast in the next phase.
end note

Proxy <-> Operator: sealed request / response\n(+ signed UsageReceipt + presigned settle group)

== 3a. Happy path — atomic settle group (operator first-half + payer ack) ==

note over Proxy, Escrow
  Atomic settle group:
    gtxn[0]  operator first-half  settle(ticketId, amountCharged,
                                          receiptDigest, asOperator=true)
              sender = node_signing (serving node's key)
              fee = (2 outer + SettleInnerCount(charged,max) + gapOpUps) * minTxnFee
              (SettleInnerCount 0..3; grouped path adds no base op-up, so a
               paid ticket = 5, a free model = 2; gapOpUps > 0 only on a
               multi-day-idle settle)
    gtxn[1]  payer ack            settle(ticketId, amountCharged,
                                          receiptDigest, asOperator=false)
              sender = t.payer,           fee = 0
              identical args to gtxn[0]
  The payer's signature on gtxn[1] is the only thing the proxy
  has to add — gtxn[0] was pre-signed by the operator. The
  asOperator arg pins each call's authorization branch so the
  same address can act in both roles when needed (e.g. operator
  testing their own deployment).
end note

Proxy -> Escrow: SubmitPresignedSettleGroup\n  decode X-Zs-Settle-Group / event: zs-settle-group\n  sign gtxn[1] in place (payer key, fee=0)\n  broadcast [gtxn[0], gtxn[1]] atomically
Escrow -> Escrow: settle() — gtxn[0] (operator first-half)\n  asOperator=true  =>  require Txn.sender == t.nodeSigning\n  load TicketRecord; status must be OPEN\n  require amount_charged <= max_price\n  require latestTimestamp <= expires_at + grace\n  record (amount, digest, pendingBy = OPERATOR)\n  status -> STATUS_PENDING_SETTLE
Escrow -> Escrow: settle() — gtxn[1] (payer ack)\n  asOperator=false =>  require Txn.sender == t.payer\n  require side != pendingBy (or args match exactly: idempotent no-op)\n  match (amount, digest) -> finalize:\n    inner-axfer payer USDC (max_price - charged - fee_paid)\n    inner-axfer operator_owner  USDC opPayout\n    inner-axfer treasury        USDC fee_paid    (skipped when 0)\n    write metrics to BOTH the (operatorId,nodeId) node box (per-node)\n      and the operatorId operator box (rollup)\n    openTickets-- (release the box-MBR slot back to the pool;\n                   NO inner ALGO refund)\n  delete TicketRecord box
Escrow --> Proxy: ok (atomic match -> box deleted)
Escrow --> Operator: USDC inner-axfer (operator owner)
Escrow --> Payer: USDC residual refund\n(box-MBR slot released to the payer's prepaid pool —\n recoverable later via withdrawMbr / closeDeposit)

note right of Operator
  Operator's settlement driver acts as a watchdog only — it
  waits hayai.settlement_watchdog_seconds (default 30s) before
  considering a standalone fire. If the box is gone (proxy
  atomic-finalized first), it records the externally-finalized
  state via MarkSettling+MarkSettled and exits. Eager firing
  is safe (idempotency tweak) but wastes ~5,000 microALGO of
  outer-fee per occurrence.
end note

== 3b. Watchdog standalone — operator fires alone after delay ==

note over Operator, Escrow
  Triggered when the proxy never broadcasts an ack (offline,
  killed, etc.) within the watchdog window. Box still exists,
  status still OPEN, no operator claim recorded yet.
end note

Operator -> Escrow: settle(ticketId, amountCharged, receiptDigest,\n                       asOperator=true)\n  sender = node_signing (serving node's key)\n  fee = (1 outer + SettleInnerCount + 1 base op-up + gapOpUps) * minTxnFee\n  (single app call always op-ups once; paid ticket = 5, free model = 2)
Escrow -> Escrow: settle() — first-half\n  status OPEN -> PENDING_SETTLE pendingBy=OPERATOR\n  records (amount, digest)
note right of Escrow
  Once status is PENDING_SETTLE pendingBy=OPERATOR with the
  operator's args, a later payer ack with matching args
  finalizes; if no payer ack arrives by deadline, anyone can
  call settleLapsed() to finalize to the operator (3c).
end note

== 3c. Lapsed path — payer never acked an operator claim ==

note over Escrow
  After latestTimestamp > expires_at + settlement_grace_seconds,
  a pending operator claim can be force-finalized. Callable
  by anyone — the operator typically posts it, but a watcher
  bot can close it out if the operator is unavailable.
end note

Operator -> Escrow: settleLapsed(ticket_id)\n  sender = any account\n  fee = (1 outer + SettleInnerCount + 1 base op-up + gapOpUps) * minTxnFee\n  (paid ticket = 5, free model = 2)
Escrow -> Escrow: settleLapsed()\n  require status == STATUS_PENDING_SETTLE\n  require pendingBy == OPERATOR\n  require latestTimestamp > expires_at + settlement_grace_seconds\n  inner-axfer payer USDC (max_price - pendingAmount - fee_paid)\n  inner-axfer operator_owner USDC opPayout\n  inner-axfer treasury USDC fee_paid (skipped when 0)\n  openTickets-- (release the box-MBR slot to the pool)\n  delete TicketRecord box
Escrow --> Operator: USDC payout
Escrow --> Payer: USDC residual refund\n(box-MBR slot released to the prepaid pool)

== 3d. Inactive path — no operator claim ever posted ==

note over Escrow
  Past the deadline, if no operator claim is pending (status is
  OPEN, or PENDING_SETTLE with pendingBy == PAYER), the payer
  recovers the full max_price (and its prepaid-pool MBR slot) via
  refundInactive. Payer pays the outer fee here (2 * minTxnFee:
  1 outer + 1 USDC refund inner) — the only ALGO-fee-bearing
  happy-ish path on the payer side (besides protest()).
end note

Proxy -> Escrow: refundInactive(ticket_id)\n  sender = any account (typically payer),  fee = 2 * minTxnFee
Escrow -> Escrow: refundInactive()\n  require status == OPEN OR\n          (status == PENDING_SETTLE AND pendingBy == PAYER)\n  require latestTimestamp > expires_at + settlement_grace_seconds\n  inner-axfer payer USDC max_price       (fee=0)\n  openTickets-- (release the box-MBR slot to the pool)\n  delete TicketRecord box
Escrow --> Payer: full USDC max_price refund\n(box-MBR slot released to the prepaid pool)

== 3e. Protest path — payer disputes receipt with evidence ==

note over Proxy
  Triggered when the proxy has cryptographic evidence
  of misbehavior (SPEC §3b): over-charge, commit_k
  mismatch, truncated stream with no refund, etc.
  Legal whether the ticket is OPEN or PENDING_SETTLE;
  silent disagreement via a mismatched second settle()
  also freezes, but protest() carries the structured
  dispute_excerpt for off-chain arbitration.

  protest() runs an in-contract ed25519verify_bare over
  the operator's receipt sig (open/settle do not — they
  authenticate via consensus)
  (1 outer + 3 OpUp inners; payer pays 4 * minTxnFee).
end note

Proxy -> Escrow: protest(ticket_id, amount_charged,\n                   receipt_digest, receipt_sig,\n                   dispute_excerpt)\n  sender = t.payer,  fee = 4 * minTxnFee
Escrow -> Escrow: protest()\n  require status in {OPEN, PENDING_SETTLE}\n  require Txn.sender == t.payer\n  ed25519verify_bare(receipt_digest, receipt_sig,\n                     t.nodeSigning.bytes)\n  require len(dispute_excerpt) <= max_dispute_excerpt_bytes\n  status -> STATUS_FROZEN\n  (no inner payments — awaits off-chain arbitration)
Escrow --> Proxy: ok
note right of Escrow
  Frozen tickets exit the auto-paths: settle(),
  settleLapsed(), and refundInactive() all reject
  STATUS_FROZEN. Resolution flows through the
  admin/arbiter path (out of scope for this diagram).
end note

note over Payer, Operator
  Terminal states per ticket: atomic match, watchdog standalone +
  later ack, settleLapsed, refundInactive (all delete the box and
  release its MBR slot to the prepaid pool), or STATUS_FROZEN (box
  retained until off-chain arbitration resolves).
end note

@enduml
